02:45:40.860 --> 02:45:42.940
I wouldn't ask too much of her, I ventured.

02:45:42.940 --> 02:45:44.940
You can't repeat the past.

02:45:44.940 --> 02:45:47.540
Can't repeat the past, he cried incredulously.

02:45:47.540 --> 02:45:49.940
Well, of course you can.

02:45:49.940 --> 02:45:54.060
He looked around him wildly as if the past were lurking here and the shadow of his house

02:45:54.060 --> 02:45:56.380
just out of reach of his hand.

02:45:56.380 --> 02:45:59.300
I'm going to fix everything just the way it was before, he said to me.

02:45:59.300 --> 02:46:01.180
I'd let him out of the past.

02:46:01.180 --> 02:46:05.460
And I gathered that he wanted to recover something, some idea of himself perhaps that had

02:46:05.460 --> 02:46:07.780
gone into loving daisy.

02:46:07.780 --> 02:46:12.260
His life had been confused and disordered since then, but if he could once return to a

02:46:12.260 --> 02:46:20.420
certain starting place and go over it all slowly, you could find out what that thing was.

02:46:20.420 --> 02:46:24.740
One autumn night, five years before, they had been walking down the street when the leaves

02:46:24.740 --> 02:46:26.020
