02:46:31.500 --> 02:46:35.140
They stopped here and turned toward each other.

02:46:35.140 --> 02:46:40.100
Now it was a cool night with that mysterious excitement in it which comes at the two changes

02:46:40.100 --> 02:46:41.500
of the year.

02:46:41.500 --> 02:46:45.860
The quiet lights in the houses were humming out into the darkness, and there was a stir

02:46:45.860 --> 02:46:48.660
and bustle among the stars.

02:46:48.660 --> 02:46:53.180
Out of the corner of his eye, Gatsby saw that the blocks of the sidewalks really formed

02:46:53.180 --> 02:46:57.420
a ladder and mounted to a secret place above the trees.

02:46:57.420 --> 02:47:02.180
He could climb to it if he climbed alone, and once there he could suck on the pap of

02:47:02.180 --> 02:47:08.580
life, gulp down the incomparable milk of wonder.

02:47:08.580 --> 02:47:13.460
His heart beat faster and faster as daisies white face came up to his own.

02:47:13.460 --> 02:47:18.540
He knew that when he kissed this girl and forever wed his unutterable visions to her perishable

02:47:18.540 --> 02:47:24.060
breath, his mind would never ramp again like the mind of God.

02:47:24.060 --> 02:47:28.620
So he waited listening for a moment longer to the tuning fork that had been struck up

02:47:28.620 --> 02:47:31.420
